## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical cache invalidation strategies in multi-region Redis deployments, testing understanding of versioned cache keys, cross-region synchronization, and TTL management. It also assesses knowledge of Redis pub/sub versus keyspace notifications and write-through caching trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Versioned cache keys with TTL management
- Cross-region invalidation patterns
- Redis pub/sub vs keyspace notifications
- Atomic operations and consistency guarantees
- Write-through vs write-behind caching strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: bumpVersion(id)
const newVer = await redis.incr(`product:${id}:ver`);
await redis.publish('cache:invalidate', JSON.stringify({id, ver: newVer}));
```

```javascript
// Pseudo: getCache(id)
const currentVer = await redis.get(`product:${id}:ver`);
const cached = await redis.get(`product:${id}:v${currentVer}`);
if (!cached) {
  // Cache miss - refresh from source
  const data = await fetchFromDatabase(id);
  await redis.setex(`product:${id}:v${currentVer}`, 120, JSON.stringify(data));
  return data;
}
return JSON.parse(cached);
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical ability to integrate REST, GraphQL, and gRPC behind a unified gateway, including automated OpenAPI generation and consistent authentication patterns.

## Key Concepts
- grpc-gateway for REST-to-gRPC translation
- OpenAPI generation from protobuf definitions
- JWT propagation through gRPC metadata
- Protocol buffer annotations for REST/GraphQL binding

## Code Example
```go
// REST to gRPC translation with grpc-gateway
func (s *server) CreateUser(ctx context.Context, req *pb.CreateUserRequest) (*pb.User, error) {
    // Forward to internal gRPC service
    return s.userService.CreateUser(ctx, req)
}

// Gateway setup with JWT propagation
func main() {
    mux := runtime.NewServeMux(
        runtime.WithIncomingHeaderMatcher(func(key string) (string, bool) {
            return key, strings.ToLower(key) == "authorization"
        }),
    )

    // Register gRPC services
    pb.RegisterUserServiceHandlerFromEndpoint(ctx, mux, "localhost:9090", []grpc.DialOption{
        grpc.WithInsecure(),
    })

    // GraphQL handler
    gqlHandler := handler.New(graphql.NewSchema())

    // Combine routers
    router := gin.Default()
    router.Any("/api/v1/*path", gin.WrapH(mux))
    router.POST("/graphql", gin.WrapH(gqlHandler))
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of token binding and multi-idp flows in production.

## Key Concepts
- Token binding with cnf
- per-tenant key rotation
- KMS/JWK management
- auditing and revocation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Issuer (simplified)
const tenantKwk = getTenantKey(tenantId); // {kid, jwk}
const token = jwt.sign({sub, iss: 'gateway', aud: tenantAud}, tenantPrivateKey, { algorithm:'ES256', header: { kid: tenantKwk.kid }, nonce: crypto.randomBytes(16).toString('hex'), cnf: { jwk: tenantKwk.jwk } });

// Verifier
const decoded = jwt.verify(token, tenantPublicKey, { algorithms:['ES256'] });
if (!compareJwk(decoded.cnf.jwk, getTenantBoundJwk(tenantId))) throw new Error('binding mismatch');
```

